  <!-- ---------------- SEO CONTENT LAYER ---------------- -->
  <section class="seo-content-section mt-12">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="seo-layout">
        
        <div class="seo-text">
          <h2 class="seo-title">Free Online Speed Reader — Flash RSVP &amp; Bionic Reading Web App</h2>
          <p>
            BriskRead is a free online speed reader for eBooks, web articles, PDFs, and textbooks at up to 1000+ words per minute (WPM). Choose one-word Flash, three-word Phrase, line-isolated Focus, fixed-anchor Flow, Bionic, or clean Page reading. Add synchronized text-to-speech when audio helps you retain context — without installing an app or creating an account.
          </p>

          <h2>How to use this online speed reader</h2>
          <ol class="seo-steps">
            <li><strong>Load text</strong> — paste an article, upload PDF/EPUB/TXT, run image OCR, extract a public URL, or use the Chrome extension.</li>
            <li><strong>Start reading</strong> — RSVP mode flashes one word at a time with Optimal Recognition Point (ORP) alignment.</li>
            <li><strong>Tune speed</strong> — set WPM from 100–1000, press Space to play/pause, and use arrow keys to jump.</li>
            <li><strong>Optional audio</strong> — enable Audio Sync for dual-channel TTS, or switch to Bionic / Standard page view.</li>
            <li><strong>Themes</strong> — light, sepia, dark, or AMOLED; press <kbd>D</kbd> to cycle.</li>
          </ol>
          
          <h2>Rapid Serial Visual Presentation (RSVP)</h2>
          <p>
            Traditional reading forces horizontal eye movement and micro-pauses (saccades). RSVP mode flashes single words at a fixed focal point. BriskRead calculates the Optimal Recognition Point of each word — the focal letter is highlighted — so your brain processes language without hunting along a line. Punctuation gets slightly longer delays so comprehension stays intact at high WPM.
          </p>
          
          <h2>Bionic Reading Mode</h2>
          <p>
            For longer sessions where you want a full page, bionic reading bolds the initial part of each word (fixations) while the rest stays lighter (saccades). Your eyes glide through paragraphs with lower load. Switch anytime between <a href="/bionic-reading">bionic reading</a>, <a href="/rsvp-reader">RSVP</a>, and standard sentence mode without reloading the document.
          </p>
          
          <h2>Dual-Channel Audio Narration &amp; PDF to speech</h2>
          <p>
            Layering TTS on visual flashes creates dual-channel focus: ears and eyes stay on the same stream. Use Chrome or Edge for neural/natural voices. Upload a PDF or EPUB and narrate client-side — see also our <a href="/pdf-to-speech">PDF to speech</a> guide. Files are parsed in the browser; optional URL extraction calls our server and AI features call Google directly with your own key, as described in the privacy policy.
          </p>

          <h2>Common use cases</h2>
          <ul class="seo-usecases">
            <li><strong>Students</strong> — revise chapters and papers faster before exams or case comps.</li>
            <li><strong>Professionals</strong> — clear newsletters, research PDFs, and long emails under time pressure.</li>
            <li><strong>Language practice</strong> — pair visual RSVP with audio to reinforce pacing.</li>
            <li><strong>Accessibility preference</strong> — choose bionic bolding, dyslexia-friendly font option, or high-contrast AMOLED.</li>
            <li><strong>Web clipping</strong> — send any public article into the reader with the Chrome extension or Extract URL.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQs Section for Structured Schema -->
        <div class="faq-container mt-12">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          
          <details class="faq-item" open>
            <summary>What is RSVP Speed Reading?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>RSVP stands for Rapid Serial Visual Presentation. It is a visual reading technology that flashes single words sequentially on a static point on the screen. This allows you to read without moving your eyes horizontally, eliminating eye muscle fatigue and significantly increasing reading speeds.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How does Bionic Reading work?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Bionic Reading highlights the first few characters of each word in bold, creating an anchor point for your eyes. Your brain instantly identifies the word based on these letters and automatically completes the rest, speeding up sentence transition and scanning speeds.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Are my PDF and EPUB files kept private?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. All parsing, document unzipping, Text-to-Speech conversions, and Image OCR happen entirely client-side inside your browser sandbox. None of your books, files, or pasted texts are uploaded to any external server.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How do I speed-read pages from Chrome?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Install the <a href="/extension">Chrome extension</a> for in-page Flash/Focus, selection reading, and read-later. You can also paste a public URL into Extract URL on the homepage.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is there an API key required for AI features?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. AI summary and document chat use your own free Gemini API key, stored only in your browser and sent straight to Google — never to our servers. Google's free tier covers normal use.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>How does multi-device Premium work?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Sign in before checkout and the one-time purchase is attached to your BriskRead account. Sign into the same account on another device to restore Premium without copying a license key.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is BriskRead really free?</summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes. Core RSVP, bionic reading, TTS, paste, and limited-length documents are free, supported by display ads. Optional Lifetime Premium ($9 one-time) removes ads, lifts the 3,000-word cap, and unlocks in-page reading in the Chrome extension.</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

